cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "A computer-certified closeness bound for the Kummer K3 surface of the Hurwitz lattice"
authors:
  - name: "Moki & Julio"
version: "1.0"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.24216647"
date-released: "2026-11-14"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Hashirama1337s/certified-kummer-k3"
license: CC-BY-4.0
keywords:
  - K3 surface
  - Kummer surface
  - Calabi-Yau metric
  - Ricci-flat metric
  - Eguchi-Hanson
  - complex Monge-Ampere equation
  - continuity method
  - computer-assisted proof
  - interval arithmetic
  - differential geometry
  - rigorous numerics
abstract: >-
  A K3 surface carries a Ricci-flat metric that exists by Yau's theorem but has no formula. For the Kummer K3 surface
  of the Hurwitz (D4) lattice, glued from a flat torus and 16 Eguchi-Hanson bubbles of size a, we prove with interval
  arithmetic that (1+d)^-1 omega_a <= omega_CY <= (1-d)^-1 omega_a for every a in (0, 0.03], with d(0.01) <= 2.851e-3,
  d(0.03) <= 0.121974 and limsup d/a^3 <= 2269.27. The qualitative estimate is due to Kobayashi (1990) and Lye (2023);
  new are the explicit certified constants and interval. Conditional on a floating-point layer assumption and standard
  facts listed in the paper. Every sealed test, including 3 FAILED, is listed. Code, data and Lean files included.
